WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.800
Dad!

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:07.630
Y-Yuuta!

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.880
Where do you think you're going
so early in the morning?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.010
Work?

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.600
It's not a place that's noisy, is it?

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.430
I have a feeling
I'm going to win today!

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.020
You are gonna play pachinko then!

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.530
THE SOMETHING BEFORE THE STORM

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.820
I should say something.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:54.990
But then...

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.950
Kidney, liver, heart...

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.660
Recently, Adachi has been acting
suspiciously, huh?

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.620
It would be unusual for Adachi
not to act suspiciously,

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.790
but it must be
because of something you've done.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:11.250
Something? Which thing, I wonder?

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.380
Adachi, you've been looking worse
than usual lately.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.220
Really?

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.220
Is your cute girlfriend
burning you up or something?

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.430
What's that?
Using your body to make a pun?

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.520
Are you okay, Adachi?
Your hand's a weird color.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.440
I-I-I-I-I'm fine.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:33.400
No, you're not fine at all!

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.150
A-da-chi!

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.070
M-M-M-M-Miyakoshi!

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.280
U-U-Uh, um...

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.450
I thought I would apologize
for the other day.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:47.960
I'm sorry you saw me pushing Higashida
down in the men's dressing room.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:54.130
Well, I'm sure you don't wanna hear
about us, so I won't get into it,

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.800
but I'll just say this...

00:02:56.210 --> 00:03:00.300
That behavior reflected my feelings towards
Higashida, and I did my best to show him.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.890
I feel much better
after apologizing. See ya!

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:05.850
Received the apology,
but doesn't feel any better.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.060
Yeah, so what do you say
at a time like this?

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.480
Oh yeah, my deepest sympathies.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:14.610
But time, place and occasion aside,
I guess that's normal dating behavior.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.280
And you'd know because you have
a girlfriend, right, Adachi?

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:20.780
We've been having
nice weather lately, huh?

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.240
<i>Kouno is being considerate of me.</i>

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.240
Kidney, liver, heart...

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:29.000
Are there any organs
you can live without?

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.710
I wonder how many organs Yuuta has?

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.840
Why are you muttering
such ghoulish things?

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.970
Saitou, what do you think
about Yuuta paying off his debt?

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:43.550
I don't think anything. Milady,
your family owns a finance company.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:48.680
After all, at this rate, I don't think
he'll ever be able to pay it off.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.900
Why don't you ask the president
to call it even?

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.980
Papa loves money and me
more than anyone else in the world.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.520
If I asked him to do that...

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:59.240
Mr. Shindou would lose
more than an organ, huh?

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:03.620
I have a good idea.
Your organs would do, right, Saitou?

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.120
Give me an organ, Saitou. An organ!

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.000
A woman of your age should not
be chanting, "Organ! Organ!"

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.420
Um, I'm sorry!

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:18.250
It seems you've been
on good terms with Saitou lately,

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.960
so why would you pull a sword on him?

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.090
After all, since that day, you haven't...

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.720
Well, I don't think
I'll be able to pay you for a while.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.890
C-C-C-Call me Shiho.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.430
<i>This woman is a pain in the butt.</i>

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.560
I'm surprised more
by Miyakoshi's manly behavior

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.820
than that scene
between Miyakoshi and Higashida.

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.820
With me and Muranushi...

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.240
Adachi...

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:44.610
Muranushi!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.990
It seems you haven't been yourself lately.
Is it because of something I've done?

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.870
You haven't done anything! I'm sorry!

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.080
I don't understand
why you're apologizing.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.830
But I see. I haven't done anything.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.920
No, nothing!

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.260
If it's not my fault, then who's at fault?

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:04.380
Oh, I've always been
a low-energy kind of guy...

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.390
Oh?

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.800
That's right. I'm fine.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.310
<i>Is she actually worried about me?</i>

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:15.150
I don't like the idea that something
other than myself can rattle you, Adachi.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.520
<i>It's not something else.</i>

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.360
Wanna go somewhere tomorrow?
It's our day off.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.070
Sure. Then let's see...

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:27.780
<i>To be honest, when you get used
to her personality, she's pretty cute.</i>

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.120
<i>It's like I can't say that it isn't
something I keep thinking about.</i>

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.120
Someone I don't know is here.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.830
<i>But it's like the two of us
hardly ever have a chance to be alone!</i>

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.580
Oh, so, about tomorrow...

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.210
You know the place, right?

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.800
Is there somewhere you'd like to go?

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:45.760
Somewhere I'd like to go?
Let's hang out at my place.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:49.220
Are you listening?

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.600
Hey, are things going well
between Adachi and Muranushi?

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:57.350
Hell if I know. Well, I think
Adachi is perfect for Muranushi,

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:01.190
except he's a shallow playboy
which makes him a loser.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.690
Which means you'd be
out of the question too, Kouno.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.400
I'm not a playboy.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:07.570
Well, it doesn't matter if she hates me.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.620
But I see. That's the type, huh?

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.200
To be honest,
it's really tough being a man.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.910
I'm sure Adachi doesn't
have that problem.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:16.330
Since he's not a man,
in more ways than one.

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.250
Hello.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:21.460
H-Hello.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.710
Y-You're here for Sis, right?

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.720
Um... Is your mom home?

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.840
You're here to see my mom?

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:29.390
No, I'm not.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.720
I just wanted to make sure.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.470
Mom's not home.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.980
<i>I'm not sure if I wanted her
to be here or not.</i>

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:40.310
U-Um, I was just leaving myself, so...
Make yourself at home.

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:41.690
Thank you!

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:45.940
Your little brother isn't like you or your mom.
Does he take after your dad?

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:47.280
Stop it.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:51.410
<i>I know Muranushi doesn't get along that well
with her mom, but her dad, too?</i>

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.620
There's more space in the living room,

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:57.660
but it's lousy with my mom's
weird hobbies, so let's go to my room.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:58.460
Um...

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:02.460
Don't be so self-conscious, Adachi.
You don't need to be scared.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.010
I decided not to set any traps today.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:08.630
"Decided not to" means you were thinking
about setting traps, huh?

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:10.840
Have some tea.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:12.300
Thanks.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:16.470
By the way, Muranushi,
why are we at your place today?

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.940
Last time you came here,
it was pretty hectic.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:20.900
I wanted to show you some hospitality.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:25.070
And depending on how things go today,
going home could be a pain, so...

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:28.780
<i>I have the feeling I know
why she invited me here.</i>

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:30.320
Wh-What do you mean by that?

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:33.580
Oh, come on, Adachi. Are you going to
make me spell it out for you?

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:36.790
When a so-called girlfriend invites
a so-called boyfriend to her house,

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.870
the reasons are limited, right?

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:42.080
For example, to talk about breaking up...

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.130
<i>I knew it!</i>

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:47.210
<i>I'm not the kind of guy someone invites over
to their room when they're in a happy-go-lucky mood!</i>

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:48.470
<i>So that's what it's about!</i>

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:52.430
You don't want other people
to hear us talking in public, right?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:56.640
You've been acting strange lately
and you said it's not my fault,

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.930
but you've been freaking out
twice as badly as usual.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.310
Knowing you, I figured
maybe you had something to say

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:03.400
but couldn't get it out because you were
thinking of my feelings.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:07.030
Muranushi, you're really
a careful observer, huh?

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:10.110
Thank you very much, Adachi.
I'm going to strangle you.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:14.950
Now, all compliments aside,
shall we continue about breaking up?

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.080
No, you've got it wrong!

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.620
I thought you wanted to dump me,

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:21.620
so when I realized I was wrong,
my mind relaxed and that slipped out!

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:25.290
I apologize for saying something
that made you anxious!

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:28.090
But I don't want to break up with you!

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:32.300
Then why have you been
acting suspicious lately, Adachi?

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.100
If you're apologizing, the least
you can do is explain yourself, right?

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.300
Otherwise...

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.470
You know?

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:40.270
<i>Her "you know" alone speaks volumes!</i>

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:43.600
<i>At this rate, she'll stab me!
But it's incredibly hard to explain!</i>

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.940
<i>I mean, when I think
about Higashida and Miyakoshi,</i>

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.480
<i>I have the feeling
that I shouldn't say it...</i>

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:49.360
I-I can't say.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:50.860
I see.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.360
PLEASE STAND BY

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:56.570
I see... Higashida and Miyakoshi...

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:59.080
<i>I really am a terrible person!</i>

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:02.710
You witnessed Miyakoshi
pushing Higashida to the floor...

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:05.330
Higashida, Miyakoshi, I'm so sorry!

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:08.090
I feel like I'm supposed to
do something here.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.800
<i>I wish I could just disappear!</i>

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:13.840
Adachi, I believe thinking about something
that's impossible is a waste of time.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.640
<i>Maybe she's gonna curse me out
from now to forever! I wanna die!</i>

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:18.680
I'm really...

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:20.390
relieved.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.640
<i>She's smiling?</i>

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:25.150
I mean, to think you were inspired
by high school students...

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.860
<i>Or rather, she's laughing at me?</i>

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:30.940
<i>Huh? Muranushi just smiled at me
right now, but I'm fine.</i>

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:33.820
<i>Because I'm used to her?
Or because it was a small smile?</i>

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:35.820
My heart's beating really fast,

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:39.870
but is it because I'm afraid like
I used to be or is it more like I'm excited?

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:45.080
My father is the kind of person who makes
a move on women using the mood,

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.080
but I don't really like that.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.960
<i>My heart is pounding like a jackhammer!</i>

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:52.760
Although my father
is neither here nor there.

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:56.010
You don't have to force yourself
to try anything out of a sense of duty.

00:09:57.050 --> 00:10:01.180
<i>Force myself... I mean,
is Muranushi's father that kind of person?</i>

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:05.190
<i>Her father is like that,
even though his wife is like that?</i>

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.980
<i>That's incredible. He's pale.
It looks like he was forcing himself.</i>

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:11.690
Adachi, your tea got cold.
Want me to pour you a new cup?

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.360
<i>But now I see.</i>

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:16.780
<i>Is that why she's pessimistic
about relationships?</i>

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.660
<i>And yet here I am,
doing nothing but making her anxious.</i>

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.120
<i>I mean...</i>

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:23.580
I...

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:25.910
I'm going home.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:30.670
How can I put it?
Adachi, you must be exhausted.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.630
I want you to get back
to your usual self soon.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.590
The Adachi who only acts
suspicious in moderation.

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:37.050
- Um...
- What?

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:40.720
Before you said, you invited me here
because going home would be a pain.

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:46.270
Do you mean it'd be a pain going home
because you'd be shocked if we broke up?

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:48.980
You're eternally insensitive, aren't you?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:53.110
Well, yes, but I don't think
we need to talk about that anymore.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:54.570
I...

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.570
Adachi?

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:56.820
Are you—

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:07.370
I-I didn't force myself to do that
or do it because of circumstances

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.420
or out of a sense of duty
or the mood of the moment,

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:10.460
so I'm not gonna apologize!

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:14.250
I'm sor... I-I'm going home!

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:26.060
<i>It was awkward having
the same shift with Muranushi today,</i>

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.770
<i>but I'm glad I came in.</i>

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.900
<i>At a glance, it doesn't look like
anything's changed with Muranushi, but...</i>

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:32.150
What?

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:34.770
What's that? Are you rattled
by what happened yesterday?

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.110
Are you mad? Are you happy?

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.650
Are you gonna stab me?

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:39.240
I wonder which one it is.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.200
What should I do?

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.240
Kidney, liver...

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.660
Is this restaurant okay?

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.090
<i>Between one thing and another,
the old man is back home.</i>

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:56.420
<i>At this rate, there'll be danger
in every direction.</i>

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:59.760
<i>I should probably turn him over
to the Kamakura family,</i>

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:02.470
<i>but then Dad's life
would likely be in danger</i>

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:04.760
<i>and I'm sure Mom would be sad.</i>

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.850
<i>But still, the way things are going now,
I'm heading towards death.</i>

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:12.600
<i>I can't... bully Shiho,</i>

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.400
<i>but our eyes just met,
so I'll try to stare her down.</i>

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:17.320
<i>No, no, can't do that!</i>

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.610
<i>If I'm not careful,
a weird feeling comes over me.</i>

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:23.160
<i>He stared at me, then looked away.</i>

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.200
Milady!

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:27.660
Wh-What is it, Saitou?
I'm busy right now!

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:30.870
I'm a newbie
and have only seen the photo...

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:33.830
but isn't he Mr. Shindou's old man?

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.790
- F-Father?
- Dad?

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.050
So it is him.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:38.840
Sorry, Yuuta.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:40.920
I intended to go in secret,
without causing any trouble,

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:43.130
but I carelessly let
a man in black catch me.

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:44.590
"Go"?

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:48.680
<i>He realized that sticking around would cause
the Kamakura family to torture me more,</i>

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:50.390
<i>so he tried to leave home again?</i>

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:53.140
<i>Honestly, I'm tortured plenty even now,
so he's wasting his time.</i>

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.400
- Where was he?
- At a pachinko parlor.

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:56.610
Die!

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.530
By the way, Yuuta...

00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:01.570
it seems we've found the person
who is responsible for the debt,

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:04.860
but I wonder why you didn't
tell me beforehand.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:06.240
Um...

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:10.080
Maybe you don't want the debt
to be paid off, Yuuta?

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.410
<i>I kind of missed this Shiho.</i>

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:16.130
<i>Why am I made to stand
in front of the jaws of death every time?</i>

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:19.920
<i>But she definitely likes me!
If I explain, she'll understand!</i>

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:22.510
Maybe if I turned
my old man over to you,

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:25.180
something could be arranged
about the debt.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:28.050
But good-for-nothing or not,
he is family,

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:30.060
and abandoning him
would make me feel bad.

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:33.520
But also, I don't think it's good to become
happy through somebody's sacrifice!

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:38.770
I think a little sacrifice is okay.

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:40.980
<i>This girl likes me too much!</i>

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.200
S-Sacrifice... Just a little sacrifice...

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.740
No, wait, what's that little smile for?

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:48.530
Let's calm down and think about this.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:52.000
With us, the stuff between our families
ties us together, right?

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.960
I can't throw that away!

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.670
Think about this... Our families...

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:00.550
I understand, Yuuta!
I totally understand!

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.300
All right! There you go, Shiho!

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:04.010
I'll abandon the Kamakura family!

00:14:05.180 --> 00:14:09.100
So I'm not going back home.
Explain it to Papa, okay?

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:10.680
W-Wait a second!

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.140
If I don't take you home,
the president will kill me!

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:14.180
It's okay.

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:16.900
You can take him home in my place.

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.770
<i>Three of us are dead!</i>

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:22.030
NEXT DAY

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.660
<i>This restaurant may be beyond saving.</i>

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.330
So I ran away from home.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:34.700
Kamakura, that's pretty reckless,
regarding safety.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:35.750
<i>Someone else's.</i>

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.580
Tell me about it!
I could be murdered at any time!

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:41.090
Kamakura, where are you going to stay?

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:45.340
She's broke and if she stayed at my place,
I'd be murdered, so it'll have to be here.

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:48.590
Doesn't living alone at a family restaurant
expose her to various dangers?

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:50.640
I'm living here with her!

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:53.970
Well, it seems you're going to
be killed, no matter what.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:54.890
Dazed...

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:55.890
Kamakura...

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:56.940
Yes?

00:14:57.140 --> 00:15:00.730
Your parents provide you with money
for living expenses, don't they?

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:04.820
Why don't you go home and think
carefully about what you want to do?

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:06.570
Go home?

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:09.280
I gave all my money
and credit cards to Saitou,

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:13.540
and I'm not receiving any more money,
so I'm pretty much flat broke.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.700
I'm surviving on what I make here.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.750
<i>This girl has courage!</i>

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:19.460
Hi there, Mr. Shindou!

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.080
Saitou!

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:23.000
I came to see how milady was doing.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:26.420
You're alive! Didn't Shiho's father
make an attempt on your life?

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:31.010
He was going to, but I stepped
out of line and threatened him

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:34.390
with "If you kill me, you won't know
where your daughter is."

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:36.770
- That takes some real courage!
- I was desperate.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.310
By the way, Saitou...
Um, what about my dad?

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.230
I'm sorry. I can't say.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.940
Changing the subject, but Mr. Shindou...

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:46.740
<i>He just swept that aside.</i>

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:48.740
Isn't the sea...

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.280
wonderful?

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.910
<i>Maybe he was drowned?</i>

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.870
I'd better wash my spare uniform.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:59.210
<i>She's too happy-go-lucky.</i>

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:04.250
<i>She used to be so crafty and cruel.
I can't believe she's become an airhead.</i>

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:07.800
<i>Maybe this is part of some plan and this
"Miss Sunshine" persona is just an act!</i>

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:09.630
By the way, Yuuta...

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:11.010
<i>Here comes her real agenda!</i>

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:14.550
What should we do next?

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:15.310
<i>No plan!</i>

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.520
Don't ask me what we should do next!

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:18.350
Okay.

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:20.390
I mean, "What should we do next?"
is the question...

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:24.020
but we need to think more seriously,
come up with an answer and then act!

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:28.440
You're right. Okay, Yuuta,
what do you think of me?

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.950
Don't put the flower back, Yuuta.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.910
For now, the happy-go-lucky stuff is over.

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:37.990
Somehow, your father has ended up
in the clutches of my family.

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:39.750
Although there's no "somehow" about it...

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:42.670
If it seems
like he's going to pay the debt,

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:45.540
then there'll be no issue
of money between us.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.460
So I'll say it once more.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:51.720
Um... Ever since I was little, Yuuta,

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.680
I-I've b-been in love with you.

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.640
<i>She seriously confessed her love to me!</i>

00:16:56.600 --> 00:17:00.480
<i>How can I put it? She's cute!
The non-sadistic Shiho is cute!</i>

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:01.980
<i>No, no, no.</i>

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:04.730
<i>I can't keep collecting death flags!</i>

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:06.560
<i>Think carefully, then act...</i>

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.070
<i>Think carefully...</i>

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.530
<i>My instincts won!</i>

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.240
That's right.

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.200
No matter which path I choose,
they're all directly connected to death,

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:23.670
so I might as well have some fun—

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:26.130
<i>Whoa, that was too close!</i>

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:27.750
<i>I almost charged down the path</i>

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:29.960
<i>that would take me
to the goal on the other side!</i>

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:34.470
U-Um... Y-Yuuta,
then you have feelings for me.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.550
Dammit. I love you.

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:39.680
P-Prove...

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:40.640
it.

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:49.900
My forehead...

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:52.940
We'll continue
after everything else is resolved.

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:54.450
This is embarrassing, dammit!

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:58.870
All right, from here on out,
what do we do?

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:00.080
Organs!

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:03.080
Don't say things that would ensure
there's no "to be continued"!

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:09.960
Adachi, you've got a dirty mind.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:13.880
Shiho, there are other people
here at the restaurant.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.800
So when we're here,
would you treat me normal?

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:18.260
Sure! Got it!

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:21.260
Don't touch me, you maggot!

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:22.680
Yeah, that's good, dammit!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.390
My... You're torturing him again!

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:26.310
Saitou...

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:28.860
What? I'm not going back home.

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:30.980
That's not why I'm here today.

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:33.150
Um, well, I'll say it in a whisper.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:35.320
It's about Mr. Shindou's dad...

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:39.660
What, did he die
after having his organs harvested?

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.580
I don't really care about that.

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.540
I don't know how to say this, but you...

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:47.580
Never mind. Anyway,
I handed him over to the president.

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.500
<i>He's purposely saying it
loud enough so I can hear.</i>

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.380
The president lectured Mr. Shindou's
dad for about eight hours.

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:56.680
Well, that shows you
how kind Papa is.

00:18:56.680 --> 00:18:58.760
After that, his dad
was on a tuna fishing boat.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.550
<i>I always thought it was just
an urban legend,</i>

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:05.020
<i>but people who are deep in debt really
are forced to go on a tuna fishing boat!</i>

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:06.390
<i>Then, with single-hook fishing...</i>

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.270
<i>Heave-ho!</i>

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:11.520
Single-hook fishing? C-Can
a novice actually fish for tuna?

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.730
He's a butcher by trade.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:14.940
Who knows?

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:20.070
Well, I'm sure he won't be able
to come home anytime soon then.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:22.450
Mom, my little brother
and sister will miss him.

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.490
No, he's back already.

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:25.790
Ahoy!

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:26.660
Dad?

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:30.790
Dad, you didn't fall into the sea, drown
and come back as a ghost, did you?

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:32.210
This is really you?

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.670
I came back safe and sound!

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:37.170
But how is it that you came back?
Has Shiho's father forgiven you?

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:41.390
I don't know if he's forgiven me,
but I caught tuna after tuna.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.180
Seriously?

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:44.810
At my age, I've finally realized
that I'm not cut out to be a butcher,

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:47.140
but I'm a natural fisherman!

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:48.690
You should've figured that out before!

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:51.980
Anyway, what a haul!
It sold for a small fortune!

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:53.230
Fortune!

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:55.980
And I thought, "Why stop there?"
so I put all that money on a horse race.

00:19:56.650 --> 00:20:00.530
Which paid off beautifully, giving me
almost enough to cover my whole debt!

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.570
But then I blew it all
on pachinko just now.

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:04.580
Dammit!

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:05.910
That hurt.

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:07.450
That's because I hit you
as hard as I could.

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:11.620
What's the difference? I can pay
the debt off later just by going fishing.

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:13.420
"Later" is a problem for me!

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:15.670
Hurry up and pay it off!
Time is of the essence!

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:18.880
What the hell? Is there some reason
you're in such a hurry?

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:22.090
That was some punch, Yuuta!

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:27.430
There's nothing better than paying off
a debt quickly, you rotten old man!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.890
<i>What was that pause just before?</i>

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:32.310
You punched me twice.

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.310
And now I'm gonna finish you off.

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:36.570
Shiho! Let me borrow your sword!

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:41.820
<i>Yuuta is doing his best to see that
the debt is paid off for our future together.</i>

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:43.160
<i>For me!</i>

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:46.830
Not flowers, the sword!

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:59.880
Miyakoshi, what's the deal
with your fingers today?

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:03.760
If I get really good at cooking...

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:14.480
I wonder if Valentine will be lonely,
since he can't meet us anymore.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:16.150
<i>Is she still on that?</i>

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:21.610
As busy as he is,
I'm sure he's looking after us too,

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:24.320
so there's no need
to worry about him, probably.

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:26.160
Really?

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:31.080
I see. Then even if I get good
at cooking...

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:32.620
If I get good at it...

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:36.330
If I get good at cooking,
it'll save your life, Higashida!

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:39.550
<i>That's all you're thinking about, huh?</i>

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:43.220
Well, we don't know
what's going to happen in the future,

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:47.300
and nothing good will come
of you thinking seriously,

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:50.220
so please just keep working
quietly day after day.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:51.770
R-Right.

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:35.950
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:29.610
And so, there's no progress whatsoever
between Higashida and Hana.

00:23:29.610 --> 00:23:31.120
<i>They're hopeless.</i>

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:32.410
Valentine is the ally of sweethearts.

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:33.990
<i>That's a cool thing to say!</i>

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:35.950
THERE'S A REASON FOR EVERYTHING

00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:35.950
Next time, "There's a Reason For Everything."
